WEBVTT

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.190
Windermere's skies...

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.150
Still...

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.170
It's been 12 hours since we arrived at Windermere.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.080
The search teams are closing in on us.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:27.920
We need to hurry.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.820
I see.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.060
Cassim Ebelhart's wind has...

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.700
The intruders hid their machines and appear to be moving on foot.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.680
I will head out and assume command myself.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.750
Roid. Keith.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.240
I have a request.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:53.970
<i>Our kiss will link us from one end to the other</i>

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:58.400
<i>Our affection is too hot for mere passionate love</i>

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.250
<i>We can be in absolute zero</i>

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.050
<i>I'll spark a dream in you</i>

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:22.570
<i>I'll embrace all you believe in</i>

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:25.190
<i>Let your genes go wild</i>

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:32.070
<i>I love you so much, but I try to play it cool sometimes</i>

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.920
<i>Tear off my mask and squeeze me to a whole new dimension</i>

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.890
<i>Our cores crash into each other, confirming our uncovered love</i>

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:47.290
<i>The tears we can't cry on our own connect us to the future</i>

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.910
<i>Our passionate love will shoot us into a super nova-like state</i>

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:59.800
<i>We can do this! No wounds can hold us back if we're together</i>

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.520
<i>Charm me with your passion, pray to the heavens</i>

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.890
<i>Our super big bang will breathe life into a new genesis</i>

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:09.150
<i>We burn our lives for this fusion</i>

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:14.630
<i>We are in absolute zero</i>

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.790
This is Delta 1.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.420
Delta 2, your status?

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.130
We are 30km away from our destination.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.520
Situation all clear.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.200
Makina, what about you?

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.410
All clear.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.930
Rei-Rei's all better too.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.580
Good as new.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.050
Their systems are still being jammed.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.060
However, they might break it any time.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.070
The enemy intercepted us with 
greater forces than expected.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:56.280
Delta 3 got separated from us and we ended up crashing far away from our destination.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:59.480
Regardless, we'll stick to the plan.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.930
Enter the royal capital of Derwent and find the system.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:06.530
We'll then use the resonance from a tactical show to destroy it.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.080
Can we really pull that off?

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.080
It's the one shot we've got.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.480
We can't tell when the song of 
the wind will be used again.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.960
Refrain from transmission until 
the next scheduled check-in.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:21.810
Out.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.860
Stop.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.510
Hide.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.780
Windermerean soldiers.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.800
Shit...

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.770
I guess we'll have to go back the way we came.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.740
This way. Come along.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:43.950
Hey!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.680
Where are we?

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.550
Only locals know this path.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.530
Is this close to your village?

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:07.180
No, it's still quite a ways from here.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.120
I used to come here to play when I was little.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.980
Back then, Earth soldiers used this area as camp.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.800
You said you got that from an Earthling.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.900
Was he one of them?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.130
Yeah. A soldier.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.030
<i>Like transparent pearls</i>

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.330
<i>tears hang in the air</i>

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:35.170
<i>I don't mind tragedy</i>

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.500
<i>just let me stay with you</i>

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.310
<i>KIRA!</i>

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.510
<i>I tag along with some meteors</i>

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.380
<i>and fall towards you...</i>

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.400
I figure everyone's making lunch right now.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:03.390
That's my village over there.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.470
I hope everyone's doing well.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.370
Freyja?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.690
I'm good.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:18.870
We need to hurry.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.380
What's that?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.390
One of the NUNS garrisons.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.100
Did you used to be stationed here?

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.070
No, but I came by a few times.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.460
We might find something useful.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.270
They're all dead.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:55.790
The 53rd Air Division was stationed here.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:06:02.410
Bunch of self-centered, over-confident pricks, but all great pilots.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.520
I found a mule we could use.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.720
Let's go.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.470
Sorry. Are you okay?

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.350
Yeah.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.320
Should we eat now while we can?

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.530
This again, Kumo-Kumo?

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:34.040
You always run off by yourself during mealtime.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:34.990
Why is that?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.900
No reason, really.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:39.920
Then let's eat together.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.260
I'll boil some water and make hot 
tea for this special occasion.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:02.400
Could it be that you're embarrassed?

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:05.650
Huh?!

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.400
I've never eaten with anyone else before.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.080
Kumo-Kumo, you're so cute!

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.290
Cute?!

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.610
She blushed!

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:20.290
Lovely.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:31.680
Is this actually edible?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.040
Sea spiders.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:34.410
Very lovely.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.750
You've lived on Ragna for 2 years 
and you've never had them?

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.930
I've been on a fixed diet.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.830
That never bothered you?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.900
I didn't really care about anything 
else as long as I could sing.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.230
Give it a try.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.280
It's pretty good!

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.010
Cold! What's this?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.950
Sea spiders are tasty.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.700
Snow's cold.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:21.310
You have plenty to learn if you don't wanna miss out.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:26.180
I love your current singing, so I can't wait to hear it once you've experienced lots more different things.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:37.780
He said he'd scout ahead, but is 
he gonna be okay on his own?

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:42.540
He would come back if anything went wrong.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.330
He'll be fine.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.620
I doubt he'd do anything stupid.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.210
You're right.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.380
You're so mature, Freyja...

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:03.680
This is your big return home, but 
you still stick to the mission.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.280
During the battle, you trusted 
Hayate and sang with all you had.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.820
Only because Mikumo scolded me.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.760
I don't know much about music,

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:22.670
but that song hit home the hardest for me.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:25.330
I could feel what you felt.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.870
It was almost painful.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.620
It was frustrating...

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.510
It was pretty frustrating for me too.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.720
You're so cool, Mirage.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:44.300
You said you'd take Hayate down if he ever lost control.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.020
I could never say that.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:51.340
In the end, I couldn't do though.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.840
But you could imagine going that far for Hayate.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.700
It really impressed me.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.660
It helped me to keep fighting.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.080
Mirage...

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.290
Freyja...

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.500
Why did you...

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.210
Why do you...

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.670
go that far...

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.710
give so much...

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.260
for Hayate—

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.260
for Hayate—

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:29.980
Hayate?

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.360
They're here. It's the Aerial Knights!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.600
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.650
We'll be fine.

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.040
Their coms are still jammed.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:48.750
What was that?

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.960
What's wrong, Bogue?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.170
I know the stench of this wind.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.130
They found us.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:01.020
Keep running!

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.140
Lord Roid, we've found three intruders!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.140
What do we do, Kumo-Kumo?

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.230
Leave this to me.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:14.940
But—

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:15.820
Hurry!

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:18.690
Counting on you!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.560
That was hot.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:40.470
Lord Roid?

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.320
You chase the other two.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:45.550
I'll send additional troops to subdue her.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.650
Da!

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.610
Damn vermin!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.710
Bogue!

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:05.280
Bogue!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.900
The White Knight.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:41.030
So you came, Star Singer.

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:44.280
Star Singer?

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.740
Rudanjal Rom Mayan.

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:28.430
You fuckers killed Cassim!

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.120
Don't do anything rash, Bogue.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.250
His Majesty wants them alive.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.880
Three intruders have been apprehended.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.510
What's your status?

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:42.440
Still pursuing them.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.460
I'll leave this to Theo and Xao.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.130
Return to the castle and report to His Majesty.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.900
Keep them captive.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:54.180
I'll join you later.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:56.870
Roger.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.440
Hey, what did you do to the village?

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.280
The people of Ravengrass?

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.170
Don't worry.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:11.270
We just checked if you were hiding there.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:25.010
Oh, them?

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:27.550
Freyja Wion.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.970
First Lt. Mirage Farina Jenius.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.890
Second Lt. Hayate Immelmann.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.860
Immelmann?

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:38.850
Lord Roid?

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.110
No way. Is that him?!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:44.030
The son of Wright Immelmann.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.160
Is that correct?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.360
Yes. He is my father.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:50.650
Control yourself.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.940
You dare came here with the 
knowledge of what your father did?

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.140
I heard about it.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:02.880
But I refuse to believe it until 
I've seen it with my own eyes.

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.480
Very well.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.680
Take him there.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.550
That's the man who took your eye?

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.910
I didn't know he was Immelmann's son.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.600
Lord Roid, do you really intend to keep them alive?

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:24.800
His Majesty wishes to hold a trial before executing them.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:31.610
Moreover, if he's so determined to see it for himself, why not let him?

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.070
We've lost contact with Mikumo?

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:37.640
And with Hayate's group as well.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.910
They might've gotten captured.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.860
Satellite tracking is still alive.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:45.170
They're all heading to Derwent.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.110
What do we do?

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.440
Stick to the plan.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.310
Meet them at the rendezvous point.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:51.130
Roger.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.940
Where are you taking us?

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:03.480
We returned Cassim's remains to his home.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.520
He should be among his family now.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:11.240
An apple was left next to him.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.830
Was that your doing?

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.740
What if it was?

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.500
Then you'd have my gratitude.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:21.460
He was a great fighter until the end.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.320
What's wrong?

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:30.880
I don't know.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:32.940
I don't know, but...

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:38.280
You said you wouldn't believe it until you saw it with your own eyes.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.650
Then behold!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.830
I've seen this before...

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.040
I see.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.640
So you've felt His Majesty's wind.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:15.680
This land was once called Karlisle.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:17.720
Karlisle?

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:23.630
Many were born here and lived here with the wind.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:24.700
But then...

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:27.070
The Dark Storm of Karlisle.

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:30.000
That's what you call it.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.490
But that was no storm.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.160
It was hell.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.430
My sister served the lord of this land.

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:45.980
My sister Mira...

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:48.420
And all the other folk...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.420
Can you still talk about justice after all this?!

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:55.170
Can you still sing for some Earthling after all this?!

00:17:55.450 --> 00:18:00.530
Can you still claim your father did nothing wrong after all this?!

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.180
Sing for them, Freyja.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.130
Hayate...

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:45.500
<i>You were always left behind,</i>

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:56.070
<i>so you just watched from where you stood</i>

00:18:56.070 --> 00:19:08.830
<i>Counting the sacrifices it takes to achieve something,</i>

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:07.720
Stop.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:18.220
<i>you just stood there hiding your tears</i>

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.520
Stop!

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:15.090
Stop! Enough singing!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:18.620
Do you think it will appease the dead?!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:27.850
<i>Your eyes are so sincere and pure,</i>

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:20.940
What good will your singing do?!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:22.780
Will it bring back the dead?!

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.350
Not even His Majesty can do that!

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.760
<i>but you never saw—</i>

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.310
Stop!

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.400
Freyja!

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:40.200
It might not do any good, but...

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:43.890
That's right. What was lost will never return.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:44.810
That is the truth.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:45.780
No!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:52.210
I don't know what's the truth, but you're all wrong!

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:54.710
My rune tells me you're all wrong!

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:56.770
She's right.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.950
What is it that you claim to know?

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:00.480
What?

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:04.060
I don't know what the truth is.

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:06.600
But I'm sure you don't know either!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.250
What do you mean?

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:12.330
What do you know about Hayate's father?

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.020
Did you see it happen with your own eyes?

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.360
Stop quibbling!

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:20.230
Do you know for sure it was Hayate's father?

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:22.160
And even if it was, do you know the reason?

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:24.200
Do you think this can ever be justified?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.070
No, but...

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.490
You guys don't know anything either!

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.080
Stop just blaming people!

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:33.540
Freyja... Mirage...

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:37.790
Lord Roid, allow me to show 
them the wings of the demon!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.640
Do as you wish.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:42.900
I leave this to you, Keith.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.550
I'll head to the sanctum.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.360
Understood.

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:49.600
Roid!

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:52.860
Was there any progress with the sanctum?

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:54.790
Yes.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.350
Everything is fine.

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:08.000
A VF-22?

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:08.490
No way...

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:12.800
These are the filthy wings that tainted our land.

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:17.960
His late Majesty King Gramia had the wreckage repaired.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:22.010
It is to serve as a reminder of our 
humiliation to all future generations.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:27.830
A pilot was found dead in the cockpit.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:36.490
Wright Immelmann, your father, was the one controlling these wings.

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:38.830
That is an undeniable fact.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:42.060
Dropping the dimensional weapon 
is also an undeniable fact.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.850
Mission 23: Scarred Requiem

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:09.050
<i>I stand on the burning wreckage</i>

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:15.770
<i>I don't know for how long or why at all</i>

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:20.530
<i>The flames around are drowning me</i>

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:27.030
<i>Finding what I seek feels so pointless now</i>

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:32.780
<i>Break the world and go beyond the ecstasy of the past</i>

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:39.160
<i>Choose the future even if it's worse than the past</i>

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.170
<i>Let's go</i>

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:43.130
<i>Love forever until the very end</i>

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:46.050
<i>Sing so hard until it hurts</i>

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:51.840
<i>Until your soul finally settles down</i>

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:54.750
<i>But if you still want to sing then</i>

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:57.580
<i>If you want to bet all on living</i>

00:22:57.580 --> 00:23:03.400
<i>The purity of your heart will destroy everything</i>

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:08.350
<i>Ah, just remember this, baby</i>

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:15.080
<i>You'll find forgiveness in a chaotic climax</i>

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:33.500
I'll devote my wings to your voice,

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.270
Star Singer.

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:39.850
Next time: Fatal Judgment
